    "result_text": "The full build succeeds. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owner creation when the lower-cased email is already used by another owner, responding with HTTP 409. Following the existing `EnsureUniqueTelephone` pattern in this OfficeFloor function-injection codebase:\n\n**New files:**\n- `EnsureUniqueEmail.java` \u2014 a pipeline step that checks the built owner's (already lower-cased by `BuildOwner`) email against the repository, skipping the optional/blank case, and throwing `DuplicateEmailException` on a conflict with a different owner.\n- `DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n- `DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 409 with a `ProblemDetail` (mirrors the telephone handler).\n- `officefloor/escalation/...DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Modified files:**\n- `OwnerRepository.java` + all three impls (`SpringDataOwnerRepository`, `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl`, `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`) \u2014 added `findByEmail`, matching case-insensitively via `LOWER(...)`.\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `ensureUniqueEmail` step (under `transaction` governance) after the telephone check.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` passes and the full test suite is green.",
